{
  // calc/ — the float math lib: a normal lib pkg whose surface lives
  // one module down (`pub mod math;` → `math.rut`). Every member is a
  // closed-union generic (`sqrt<T requires f32 | f64>`) — the width
  // falls out of the argument, no suffix to spell. The body is the
  // `is` dispatch: `x is f32` folds per member (generic bodies compile
  // per instantiation) and the if's dead-arm pruning drops the other
  // row's call, so each member's body is ONE host call into
  // `calc_host` (whose rows carry the width in their internal names).
  // The closed union is what makes the delivery finite: the pack
  // enumerates every member as a pack-time ledger instantiation, so a
  // consumer's `sqrt<f32>` request is served from the ledger — no
  // template row, no placeholder compile.
  //
  // Callers bind the module and qualify: `use calc::{ math }` then
  // `math::sqrt(x)` / `math::PI` — or the fully-qualified
  // `calc::math::sqrt(x)` with no use. The CONSTANTS are calc_host's
  // SURFACE LETS (`pub let PI: f64 = ..;` in its calc.d.rut — the
  // manifest's `consts` key is retired), re-exported through math's
  // `pub use calc_host::{ PI, .. }` — callers never touch the host
  // pkg. The INTEGER numeric methods (`wrapping_*`, `saturating_*`,
  // `checked_*`) are core's `builtin impl` methods; `NAN` is core's
  // too (`use core::{ NAN }`).
  "name": "calc",
  "deps": {
    "calc_host": {
      "path": "../calc_host"
    }
  }
}
